---
import EditorialCase from './EditorialCase.astro';
import StoryChapter from './StoryChapter.astro';
import StoryFocus from './StoryFocus.astro';
import BuzzvilScale from './BuzzvilScale.astro';
import OfferwallNetwork from './OfferwallNetwork.astro';
import OfferwallCarousel from './OfferwallCarousel.astro';
import OfferwallSystem from './OfferwallSystem.astro';
import type { WorkEntry } from '../../data/work';
interface Props { work: WorkEntry }
const { work } = Astro.props;
const tests = [
  { label: 'Ads shown per visit', before: '6.88', after: '7.96', beforeWidth: 77.4, afterWidth: 89.6, change: '+16%', note: 'More offers were exposed.' },
  { label: 'Revenue / 1,000 visits', before: '12.87', after: '13.77', beforeWidth: 84.1, afterWidth: 90, change: '+7%', note: 'Each visit generated more revenue.' },
  { label: 'Share of ads clicked', before: '8.54%', after: '7.49%', beforeWidth: 90, afterWidth: 78.9, change: '−12%', note: 'Exposure did not translate equally into clicks.' },
];
const lessons = [
  { title: 'Design the connections.', body: 'The Feed became more valuable when the units around it had a clear route into it. My scope grew from individual screens to the network of connected ad placements.' },
  { title: 'Let the publisher own the context.', body: 'A shared destination did not require identical placements. Integration guidance gave publishers room to adapt the carousel while keeping its connection to the Feed.' },
  { title: 'Read beyond the uplift.', body: 'Impressions, visits, revenue and engagement answer different questions. Their tradeoffs were more useful than a single headline number.' },
];
---
<EditorialCase
  work={work}
  headline={'Connecting campaigns\nthrough the Offerwall.'}
  intro="An Offerwall brings together campaigns and offers where people earn rewards. I connected campaign placements across our partner companies’ apps to this shared destination, first as a designer and later as product owner. Internally, we called it Feed, then Hub."
  role="I started as a hands-on designer, then spent about two years in supply product ownership and management. As product manager and designer, I shaped the ‘1 feed 4 all’ strategy, the SDK and its entry points, alongside engineering and the wider product team."
  coverNote="Reimagined product scenes with fictional campaigns and rewards."
  websites={[{ label: 'Current Offerwall documentation', url: 'https://docs.buzzvil.com/docs/buzzbenefit-android/v6/benefithub' }, { label: 'Honeyscreen · live app', url: 'https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.buzzvil.adhours&hl=en_US' }]}
  lessons={lessons}
>
  <Fragment slot="cover"><OfferwallNetwork /></Fragment>

  <BuzzvilScale stage="offerwall" />

  <div class="offerwall-story">
    <StoryChapter id="offerwall-system" scope="The product foundation" title={'One product had to feel\nat home in many apps.'} intro="Hundreds of interfaces had to fit inside hundreds of different apps. I built much of the early design system around that challenge: keep a shared product, while letting each partner’s brand shape how it looks and feels." class="system-chapter">
      <OfferwallSystem />
      <p class="system-scope">Phantom, Chameleon and the systems that followed were successive attempts at the same problem. We rebuilt and refined our UI kits through hundreds of iterations. From the start, the ambition was a headless design system: separate the product’s behavior from its visual identity, with design decisions expressed as tokens or configurable values for each brand.</p>
      <StoryFocus topic="Where the brand decisions live" problem="A new brand should change the design values, without requiring a separate version of every screen.">
        <div class="token-model">
          <div class="token-model-heading"><h3>Two layers today.<br/>A third layer to grow into.</h3><p>Tokens are named design values. Separating the raw values from their purpose lets the same interface take on a different identity.</p></div>
          <ol class="token-layers">
            <li><span class="token-state">In the SDK today</span><h4><span>01</span> Core</h4><p>The raw material: colors, spacing and other foundational values.</p><div class="token-example"><div class="token-swatches" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><span>A brand’s color palette</span></div></li>
            <li><span class="token-state">In the SDK today</span><h4><span>02</span> Semantic</h4><p>What those values mean: a primary action, a background or readable text.</p><div class="token-example"><strong class="semantic-example">Primary action</strong><span>A shared role, a brand-specific value</span></div></li>
            <li class="token-future"><span class="token-state">A next step</span><h4><span>03</span> Component</h4><p>How a particular element uses those roles, allowing more precise control.</p><div class="token-example"><strong class="component-example">Claim reward</strong><span>For example, a reward button’s background</span></div></li>
          </ol>
          <p class="token-model-note">The layers, illustrated. Component-specific tokens remain a direction to develop.</p>
        </div>
      </StoryFocus>
      <div class="decision-strip"><h3>The system kept growing.<br/>So did its flexibility.</h3><p>The team continued this work after my early systems. Today’s SDK has a solid core-and-semantic token foundation and a full server-driven interface, configured from the server. I would like to take it further with component-specific tokens, so individual elements can adapt without changing a shared role everywhere.</p></div>
      <details class="originals"><summary>Inside the original system · 2021</summary><div class="archive-pair"><figure><img src="/work/offerwall/feed-2021.webp" width="375" height="812" alt="2021 Feed prototype with tabs, filters, image and video cards" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/><figcaption>The full Feed: a hierarchy for navigation, creative and reward.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="/work/offerwall/feed-bottomsheet-2021.webp" width="360" height="740" alt="2021 Feed component system adapted to a bottom sheet" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/><figcaption>The same hierarchy inside a bottom sheet, with publisher context behind it.</figcaption></figure></div><p>Original designs with sample campaigns and rewards.</p></details>
    </StoryChapter>

    <StoryChapter id="offerwall-carousel" scope="Zoom in · Connecting campaigns to more offers" title={'A row of campaigns became\na way into more offers.'} intro="The shared Feed needed ways in from the campaigns people already encountered. One example was the carousel I created: a horizontally scrolling row of campaign cards inside a partner’s app, with a link and final card that opened the wider Feed." class="carousel-chapter">
      <OfferwallCarousel />
      <div class="decision-strip"><h3>We kept the connection.<br/>Publishers shaped the placement.</h3><p>A bundled carousel UI made customization too heavy. We moved to an integration guide and sample implementation, with SDK support for the final Feed-promotion card.</p></div>
      <details class="originals"><summary>Compare the original carousel</summary><figure><img src="/work/offerwall/carousel-to-feed.webp" width="837" height="772" alt="Original Honeyscreen designs showing a native ad and the final Feed promotion card in the same carousel placement" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/><figcaption>The original design: a final card opens the Feed. Sample rewards.</figcaption></figure><a href="https://www.figma.com/design/45kZV5TgUKYV5LURmTXrQO?node-id=1-2269">Original Carousel UI file</a></details>
    </StoryChapter>

    <StoryChapter id="offerwall-evidence" title={'Exposure grew. Engagement\nstill needed work.'} intro="Connecting the units drove substantial Feed-impression growth. As product owner, I also needed to understand its limits: the overall product, a layout test and one carousel placement told different stories." class="evidence-chapter">
      <div class="scale-board">
        <div class="scale-context"><span class="eyebrow">Feed product totals / 2021</span><h3>The Feed grew<br/>across platforms.</h3><p>May–June compared with July–August 2021.<br/>Two-month totals across all platforms.</p></div>
        <div class="scale-numbers"><div><span>Feed page views</span><p><small>392.0M</small><strong>432.2M</strong></p></div><div><span>Feed revenue</span><p><small>₩3.37B</small><strong>₩3.61B</strong></p></div></div>
        <p class="scale-boundary">Wider publisher adoption contributed to this growth. These totals describe the product; they do not isolate the effect of a redesign.</p>
      </div>
      <StoryFocus topic="Feed density" problem="Growing exposure was not enough. Could a different layout turn more of those visits into advertiser value?">
      <div class="experiment-board">
        <header><div><span class="eyebrow">Feed layout A/B / 2022</span><h3>More ads shown. More revenue.<br/>A smaller share clicked.</h3></div><div class="chart-legend"><span><i></i>Original</span><span><i></i>Revised</span></div></header>
        <div class="metric-grid">{tests.map(test=><div class="metric"><span class="metric-label">{test.label}</span><strong class="metric-change">{test.change}</strong><div class="paired-bars" aria-label={`${test.label}: original ${test.before}, revised ${test.after}.`}><div><i style={`width:${test.beforeWidth}%`}></i><span>{test.before}</span></div><div><i style={`width:${test.afterWidth}%`}></i><span>{test.after}</span></div></div><p>{test.note}</p></div>)}</div>
        <p class="experiment-finding">Showing more ads increased revenue per visit, but a smaller share of those ads were clicked. A more prominent action button did not close the gap. There was no difference in people returning the next day or the following week.</p>
        <p class="source-note"><a href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.buzzvil.adhours&hl=en_US">Honeyscreen</a>, Buzzvil’s rewards app · Android, 2022. Rounded changes; each chart uses its own scale. Design: Brice, Diane and Max. Analysis: Cathie. <a href="https://buzzvil.atlassian.net/wiki/pages/2701525706">Analysis</a></p>
      </div>
      </StoryFocus>
      <StoryFocus topic="The carousel’s connection to Feed" problem="The carousel introduced more campaigns, but did people continue to the shared destination?">
      <div class="carousel-result"><div><span class="eyebrow">Separate carousel analysis</span><p class="exposure-ratio"><span>1</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i><strong>2.7</strong></p><span>Ads shown each time the placement appeared</span></div><div><h3>More cards seen.<br/>Not more Feed visits.</h3><p>Visits from these campaign cards to the Offerwall stayed broadly flat. The carousel increased exposure within this placement; that is a different result from the growth of the connected ecosystem.</p><p class="source-note">Honeyscreen Android, 2022. Before/after comparison for this placement, not the whole network. <a href="https://buzzvil.atlassian.net/wiki/pages/2748481537">Analysis</a></p></div></div>
      </StoryFocus>
    </StoryChapter>

    <StoryChapter id="offerwall-boundary" scope="Back to the product · The next constraint" title={'A bigger Hub exposed the\nlimits of a single feed.'} intro="The team continued the ecosystem after I moved on. By 2025–2026, adding more formats meant competing for the same attention: moving one section up could move another out of sight." class="boundary-chapter">
      <div class="boundary-layout"><div class="boundary-copy"><p>Requiring partner apps to have their own points system also limited who the product could serve. The next questions were about the experience itself, and what would make people participate.</p><a class="next-case" href="/work/game-ua-multi-mission/">Continue with Game UA</a></div>
      <figure class="reach-board"><figcaption><span>Later finding · Visibility within the page</span><b>KB StarBanking</b></figcaption><div class="reach-row"><div><span>Upper sections</span><strong>93–95%</strong></div><div class="reach-bar"><i style="width:94%"></i></div></div><div class="depth-indicator" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><span>Further down the same Hub</span><i></i></div><div class="reach-row lower"><div><span>Shopping</span><strong>11%</strong></div><div class="reach-bar"><i style="width:11%"></i></div></div><p>Share of Hub visitors who saw each section. Later team research.</p><a href="https://buzzvil.atlassian.net/wiki/pages/5100503176">Read the team’s findings</a></figure>
      </div>
    </StoryChapter>
  </div>
</EditorialCase>

<style>
.token-model-heading { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.2fr; gap: 2rem; align-items: start; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
.token-model-heading h3 { margin: 0; font: 400 clamp(1.5rem,2.8vw,2.2rem)/1.25 var(--font-body); letter-spacing: -.035em; }
.token-model-heading p { margin: 0; font: .95rem/1.75 var(--font-body); color: var(--theme-text-muted); }
.token-layers { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr)); gap: 1rem; list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
.token-layers li { display: flex; flex-direction: column; padding: clamp(1rem,2vw,1.6rem); border: 1px solid var(--theme-border); background: color-mix(in srgb,var(--theme-text) 3%,var(--theme-bg)); min-width: 0; }
.token-layers li.token-future { border-style: dashed; background: none; }
.token-state { font: .65rem/1.5 var(--font-mono); color: var(--theme-text-muted); }
.token-layers h4 { margin: 1.2rem 0 .8rem; font: 400 1.35rem/1.4 var(--font-body); }
.token-layers h4>span { font: .7rem/1.4 var(--font-mono); color: var(--theme-text-muted); margin-right: .65rem; }
.token-layers p { margin: 0 0 1.5rem; font: .85rem/1.7 var(--font-body); color: var(--theme-text-muted); }
.token-example { margin-top: auto; border-top: 1px solid var(--theme-border); padding-top: 1.25rem; min-height: 100px; }
.token-example>span { display: block; margin-top: .8rem; font: .7rem/1.5 var(--font-body); color: var(--theme-text-muted); }
.token-swatches { display: flex; gap: .4rem; }
.token-swatches i { width: 30px; height: 30px; border-radius: 50%; background: #356253; border: 1px solid #8ba89a; }
.token-swatches i:nth-child(2) { background: #a9c8b8; }
.token-swatches i:nth-child(3) { background: #edf2e9; }
.semantic-example { display: inline-block; font: 500 .85rem/1.5 var(--font-body); color: #b9d9c6; border-left: 3px solid #a9c8b8; padding: .25rem .6rem; }
.component-example { display: inline-block; background: #a9c8b8; color: #18372c; padding: .5rem .8rem; border-radius: 5px; font: 500 .8rem/1.4 var(--font-body); }
.token-model-note { font: .75rem/1.6 var(--font-body); color: var(--theme-text-muted); margin: 1rem 0 0; }
@media(max-width:700px) { .token-model-heading,.token-layers { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .token-model-heading { gap: 1rem; } .token-example { min-height: 0; } }

.system-scope{max-width:68ch;margin:1.5rem 0;font:1rem/1.8 var(--font-body,sans-serif);color:var(--theme-text-muted)}
.source-note{font:12px/1.7 var(--font-body,sans-serif);color:var(--theme-text-muted)}
.offerwall-story{min-width:0}.eyebrow{display:block;font:10px/1.5 var(--font-mono,monospace);letter-spacing:.09em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--theme-text-muted);margin-bottom:18px}.boundary-copy>p{font:15px/1.8 var(--font-mono,monospace);color:var(--theme-text-muted);margin:0;max-width:43ch}.decision-strip{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.1fr;gap:30px;padding:28px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--theme-border);margin-top:22px}.decision-strip h3{font:400 20px/1.35 var(--font-mono,monospace);letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:0}.decision-strip p{font:15px/1.8 var(--font-body,sans-serif);color:var(--theme-text-muted);margin:0}.originals{margin-top:22px;font:11px/1.7 var(--font-mono,monospace);color:var(--theme-text-muted)}.originals summary{width:fit-content;cursor:pointer;padding:7px 0}.originals summary:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--theme-text);outline-offset:4px}.originals figure{max-width:720px;margin:22px auto}.originals img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}.originals figcaption{margin-top:12px}.originals a,.source-note a,.reach-board>a,.next-case{color:var(--theme-text);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:4px}.archive-pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:35px;max-width:650px;margin:25px auto}.archive-pair figure{margin:0}.archive-pair img{max-width:375px}.scale-board{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.5fr;gap:30px;background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--theme-text) 4%,var(--theme-bg));padding:clamp(22px,4vw,44px);margin-bottom:32px}.scale-context h3{font:400 22px/1.3 var(--font-mono,monospace);letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:0 0 18px}.scale-context p{font:13px/1.8 var(--font-body,sans-serif);color:var(--theme-text-muted)}.scale-numbers{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:30px;align-self:center}.scale-numbers>div>span{font:12px/1.6 var(--font-mono,monospace);color:var(--theme-text-muted)}.scale-numbers p{margin:18px 0 0}.scale-numbers small{display:block;font:18px/1.3 var(--font-mono,monospace);color:var(--theme-text-muted);margin-bottom:7px}.scale-numbers strong{display:block;font:400 clamp(26px,4.5vw,46px)/1.1 var(--font-mono,monospace);letter-spacing:-.07em}.scale-boundary{grid-column:1/-1;font:12px/1.8 var(--font-body,sans-serif);color:var(--theme-text-muted);margin:0;padding-top:20px;border-top:1px solid var(--theme-border)}.experiment-board{padding:clamp(22px,4vw,44px);border:1px solid var(--theme-border)}.experiment-board>header{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:25px;align-items:end;margin-bottom:40px}.experiment-board h3{font:400 clamp(19px,3vw,29px)/1.35 var(--font-mono,monospace);letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:0}.chart-legend{display:flex;gap:18px;flex-shrink:0;font:9px/1.5 var(--font-mono,monospace);color:var(--theme-text-muted)}.chart-legend>span{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px}.chart-legend i{display:block;width:7px;height:7px;background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--theme-text) 22%,transparent)}.chart-legend>span:last-child i{background:var(--theme-text)}.metric-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:32px}.metric-label{display:block;font:12px/1.6 var(--font-mono,monospace);color:var(--theme-text-muted)}.metric-change{display:block;font:400 clamp(25px,4.5vw,43px)/1.1 var(--font-mono,monospace);letter-spacing:-.055em;margin:16px 0 22px}.paired-bars{display:grid;gap:10px}.paired-bars>div{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px}.paired-bars i{display:block;flex-shrink:1;height:7px;background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--theme-text) 22%,transparent)}.paired-bars>div:last-child i{background:var(--theme-text)}.paired-bars span{font:9px/1 var(--font-mono,monospace);color:var(--theme-text-muted);flex-shrink:0}.metric>p{font:13px/1.7 var(--font-body,sans-serif);color:var(--theme-text-muted);margin:20px 0 0}.experiment-finding{font:14px/1.8 var(--font-mono,monospace);max-width:65ch;margin:35px 0 16px;padding-top:25px;border-top:1px solid var(--theme-border)}.experiment-board .source-note{font-size:12px;max-width:90ch;margin-bottom:0}.carousel-result{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.3fr;gap:55px;padding:40px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--theme-border)}.exposure-ratio{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:18px;font:400 clamp(40px,6vw,70px)/1 var(--font-mono,monospace);letter-spacing:-.06em;margin:26px 0 17px}.exposure-ratio>span{color:var(--theme-text-muted)}.exposure-ratio>strong{font-weight:400}.exposure-ratio i{height:1px;width:30px;background:var(--theme-text-muted)}.carousel-result>div>span:last-child{font:10px/1.6 var(--font-mono,monospace);color:var(--theme-text-muted)}.carousel-result h3{font:400 25px/1.3 var(--font-mono,monospace);letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:0 0 18px}.carousel-result>div>p:not(.exposure-ratio){font:15px/1.8 var(--font-body,sans-serif);color:var(--theme-text-muted)}.carousel-result>div>p.source-note{font-size:12px}.boundary-layout{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:clamp(30px,8vw,95px);align-items:center}.boundary-copy>p{font:1rem/1.8 var(--font-body,sans-serif);margin:0 0 24px}.next-case{display:inline-block;font:12px/1.7 var(--font-mono,monospace);margin-top:8px}.reach-board{margin:0;padding:30px;background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--theme-text) 4%,var(--theme-bg));font-family:var(--font-mono,monospace)}.reach-board>figcaption{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;padding-bottom:26px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--theme-border);font-size:10px;color:var(--theme-text-muted)}.reach-board>figcaption>b{font-weight:400;color:var(--theme-text);font-size:15px}.reach-row{margin-top:30px}.reach-row>div:first-child{display:flex;align-items:baseline;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px}.reach-row span{font-size:11px;color:var(--theme-text-muted)}.reach-row strong{font-size:28px;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:-.05em}.reach-bar{height:8px;background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--theme-text) 8%,transparent);margin-top:13px}.reach-bar i{display:block;height:100%;background:var(--theme-text)}.depth-indicator{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:12px;margin:22px 0;color:var(--theme-text-muted);font-size:9px}.depth-indicator i{height:25px;width:1px;background:var(--theme-border)}.lower{margin-top:0}.reach-board>p{font:12px/1.8 var(--font-body,sans-serif);color:var(--theme-text-muted);margin:25px 0 12px}.reach-board>a{font-size:10px}.offerwall-story a:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--theme-text);outline-offset:4px}
@media(max-width:800px){.decision-strip{grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr}.scale-board{grid-template-columns:1fr}.scale-context h3{max-width:26ch}.scale-numbers{gap:40px}.scale-numbers strong{font-size:42px}.experiment-board>header{align-items:start;flex-direction:column}.metric-grid{gap:20px}.boundary-layout{gap:32px}.reach-board{padding:24px}.carousel-result{gap:30px}}
@media(max-width:560px){.decision-strip{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:18px}.archive-pair{gap:18px}.originals{font-size:10px}.scale-board{gap:20px}.scale-numbers{gap:20px}.scale-numbers strong{font-size:34px}.scale-numbers small{font-size:15px}.scale-context h3{font-size:21px}.metric-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:28px}.metric{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:13px 20px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--theme-border);padding-bottom:24px}.metric:last-child{border-bottom:0;padding-bottom:0}.metric-label{grid-column:1/-1}.metric-change{margin:0;font-size:35px}.paired-bars{align-self:center}.metric>p{grid-column:1/-1;margin:0}.experiment-board>header{margin-bottom:30px}.experiment-finding{font-size:12px}.carousel-result{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:26px}.exposure-ratio{font-size:56px;margin:20px 0 12px}.boundary-layout{grid-template-columns:1fr}.boundary-copy>p{max-width:unset}.reach-board{padding:26px}.reach-row strong{font-size:34px}}
</style>
